<!-- ================================ LEDGER ================================ -->
<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">The Ledger</p>
    <h2 id="t-what-holds-up-and-what-does-not">What Holds Up, and What Does Not</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Survives</h3>
      <ul class="biblio">
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> <strong>The three fractions, and their error bars.</strong>
        68.9 / 26.2 / 4.9 at the present epoch, from independent methods that agree.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> <strong>The mixture changes with time.</strong> Radiation,
        matter and the cosmological constant dilute as a&#8315;&#8308;, a&#8315;&#179; and not at all. No
        doctrine needed for this; it is the expansion.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> <strong>The coincidence problem is real and open.</strong>
        Saying so is not a concession to mysticism; it is the state of the field.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> <strong>Couplings run.</strong> Measured at colliders, and the
        running is predicted by the Standard Model to high precision.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> <strong>Measurement disturbs; information is physical.</strong>
        No-cloning, the Heisenberg relations and Landauer's limit are all real, and all genuinely limit
        what can be recovered about a past collapse.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Does Not Survive</h3>
      <ul class="biblio">
        <li><span class="myth">&#9670;</span> <strong>"Constants are accumulated residue."</strong> Every
        measurement to date says the constants have not moved: &#124;&#945;&#775;/&#945;&#124; below
        10&#8315;&#185;&#8312; per year. A framework that needs drift must explain why none is seen.</li>
        <li><span class="myth">&#9670;</span> <strong>"The ledger sets 68.9 / 26.2 / 4.9."</strong> No
        number has yet been derived from it. Until one is, the mapping is a picture laid over an answer
        obtained elsewhere.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> <strong>"It cannot be quantised, therefore it is real."</strong>
        Unmeasurability is not evidence. A quantity defined so that no experiment can touch it is also a
        quantity no experiment can support.</li>
        <li><span class="myth">&#9670;</span> <strong>Dark matter as unphased residue.</strong> Dark matter
        clusters, lenses and falls like cold, collisionless mass. Any story about it must reproduce that
        behaviour in detail, and this one does not yet try.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> <strong>"Collapse requires an observer."</strong> It does
        not, and the Ledger must be stated in terms of decoherence rather than observation if it is to
        survive its first referee.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

